-- Bookings: a studio with one room sells it by the hour over the counter. A
-- walk-in books a slot now and either holds it or learns it is taken; someone
-- who wanted a taken slot leaves a name, and is told hourly once the slot
-- comes free. The sixteenth Velle spec, written to show what runs at the same
-- time and what takes turns (the wiki guide Concurrency): two bookings of one
-- slot must take turns, two bookings of two slots must not wait for each
-- other, and the hourly waitlist sweep must not stop the counter.
--
-- What the domain asks of the language, and where each answer lives:
--   · one slot, one booking — a prohibition over the booking the rule creates
--     (Reference §21); the compiler keys the booking's commit on the slot the
--     request carries, so two bookings of one slot take turns and the second is
--     refused, while bookings of two slots run together
--   · cancelling frees the slot — the cancellation is a fact on the booking,
--     which stays on record (Reference §12); the slot is free when no booking
--     still standing holds it, and the commit is keyed on the booking cancelled
--   · the waitlist is told hourly — a scheduled rule whose condition reads the
--     bookings of one slot (Reference §17); each firing is a commit of its own,
--     keyed on the entry and on the slot it waits for
--   · a cap over the whole waitlist — a prohibition reading every entry, which
--     makes every joining commit wait for every other; the width is declared
--     deliberate with `tolerates contention` (checks A5)
--
-- Comment convention (as in payments.velle): plain comments tell the business
-- story; `velle:` comments note the language machinery on show.

-- ── Booking a slot ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- A walk-in asks for a slot. The request is decided at its own commit and not
-- kept: the booking is the record.
transient act BookNow {
    slot: DateTime
    bookedFor: text
}

-- The booking of one slot. A cancelled booking stays on record, with its
-- cancellation beside it.
shape Booking {
    slot: DateTime
    bookedFor: text
    bookedOn: timestamp on create
}

shape Cancellation {
    booking: one Booking
    cancelledOn: timestamp on create
}

-- A booking still standing.
shape StandingBooking = Booking where not exists (Cancellation where booking == this)

-- No two standing bookings hold one slot.
-- velle: a prohibition over the record the rule creates. The commit that
-- creates it is keyed on the slot, read off the request before the rule runs,
-- so two requests for one slot take turns and the second meets the first's
-- booking; requests for different slots do not wait for each other.
never (StandingBooking where exists (StandingBooking as other where other.slot == this.slot and not (other == this)))

rule Book when BookNow {
    Booking from { slot: slot, bookedFor: bookedFor }
}

-- ── Cancelling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- The holder gives the slot back. The booking stays, marked cancelled.
transient act Cancel {
    booking: one Booking
}

-- A booking is given back once at most.
-- velle: a constraint on the booking, holding at the end of the cancellation's
-- commit; the second cancellation of one booking is refused with the first on
-- record.
never (Booking where count(cancellations) > 1)

-- velle: the commit is keyed on the booking it cancels, so a cancellation waits
-- only for work on that booking.
rule ApplyCancel when Cancel {
    Cancellation from { booking: booking }
}

-- ── The waitlist ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- Someone who wanted a taken slot leaves a name. The entry is a record the
-- hourly sweep reads.
act Waitlist {
    slot: DateTime
    name: text
}

-- The waitlist holds at most twenty names.
-- velle: the count reads every entry and ties to no one of them, so every
-- joining commit takes turns with every other joining commit. That is the
-- intended price of a cap over the whole list, and `tolerates contention`
-- says so; without it the compiler warns (checks A5).
never (Waitlist where count(Waitlist) > 20) tolerates contention

-- An entry whose slot is free, and one that has not been told yet.
shape Unserved = Waitlist where not exists (StandingBooking where slot == this.slot)
shape Untold = Unserved where not exists (Notice where entry == this)

-- The hourly word that the slot is free.
shape Notice {
    entry: one Waitlist
    sentOn: timestamp on create
}

-- velle: each firing is a commit of its own, keyed on the entry and on the
-- slot's bookings. A booking of that slot arriving during the sweep takes its
-- turn against this one firing; bookings of other slots do not wait. An entry
-- is told once: a slot booked and freed again after the notice is not re-told.
rule TellWaitlist when Untold on Hourly {
    Notice from { entry: this }
}
